#: ../../../install_windows.md:5
msgid "Binary Installation on Windows 10/11"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:7
msgid ""
"Binaries for all the dependencies used by Gazebo can be found in the [conda-"
"forge](https://conda-forge.org/) package repository. The Gazebo buildfarm "
"and these instructions use the [Pixi](https://pixi.sh/) package manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:10
msgid "Install dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:12
msgid ""
"Follow the Pixi installer instructions from https://pixi.sh/latest/ to "
"install pixi. Once pixi has been installed, close the terminal session and "
"start it again, which will ensure pixi is on the PATH."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:16
msgid ""
"Make a folder to initialize the Pixi project.  Just make sure that the "
"directory does not contain any spaces. Open up a command prompt and type the "
"following"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:19
msgid ""
"   cd C:\\Users\\%USERNAME%\\ \n"
"   mkdir gz-ws\n"
"   cd gz-ws\n"
"   pixi init\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:25
msgid "You should see this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:27
msgid "   ✔ Created C:\\Users\\USER\\ws_gz\\pixi.toml\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:31
msgid ""
"Prepare the pixi.toml file Now that the Pixi environment has been installed, "
"you can add the packaged gazebo binary to it and some necessary environment "
"variables for the QT library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:34
msgid "Open up the pixi.toml file in your editor of choice or simple notepad."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:36
msgid "notepad pixi.toml\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:40
msgid "Replace `[dependencies]` with the following in the pixi.toml file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:42
msgid ""
"[target.win-64.activation.env]\n"
"QT_QPA_PLATFORM_PLUGIN_PATH=\"%CONDA_PREFIX%\\\\Library\\\\lib\\\\qt6\\"
"\\plugins\\\\platforms\"\n"
"QML2_IMPORT_PATH=\"%CONDA_PREFIX%\\\\Library\\\\lib\\\\qt6\\\\qml\"\n"
"\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"gz-sim = \"9.*\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:51
msgid ""
"Save and close the pixi.toml file, and then let Pixi pull all the "
"dependencies and install Gazebo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:53
msgid "pixi install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:56
msgid "You should be seeing this"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:58
msgid "✔ The default environment has been installed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:62
msgid "You should now be able to launch gazebo normally within a pixi shell:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:64
msgid ""
"pixi shell\n"
"gz sim -v4 -s shapes.sdf\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:69
msgid "And in a second terminal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:71
msgid ""
"pixi shell\n"
"gz sim -g\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:76
msgid ""
"Note, Gazebo Harmonic has a bug that it can not run the simulator in one "
"session, it needs to be launched with the server and gui separately. This "
"bug has been fixed in later versions of Gazebo (Jetty and up)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:78
msgid ""
"This is the end of the binary install instructions; head back to the "
"[Getting started](getstarted) page to start using Gazebo!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:80
msgid "Uninstalling binary-based gazebo install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:82
msgid ""
"Uninstalling the Gazebo binary is as simple as removing the full folder that "
"was created with the Pixi environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:84
msgid ""
"In a command prompt, navigate to the root directory of where the folder is "
"(depending on the location you chose at the first step), and remove it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_windows.md:86
msgid ""
"   cd C:\\Users\\%USERNAME%\\ \n"
"   rmdir /s /q gz-ws\n"
msgstr ""

